    "task":  "Live-playtest polish session on GTFO.AbsurdWeapons: user is actively playing the game while I make rapid fixes/tweaks. Most recently added a continuous loop sound to the Shrink Beam (Sounds.cs ShrinkLoopStart/ShrinkLoopStop = BIOTRACKER_TOOL_LOOP/BIOTRACKER_TOOL_LOOP_STOP, wired into ShrinkStream.Spawn via LoopSounds.Touch) - built, deployed, 39/39 tests pass, left UNCOMMITTED pending the users in-game confirmation it sounds right.",
    "decisions":  "Workflow established this session: (1) game runs continuously and often locks GTFO.AbsurdWeapons.dll - verify compilation with `dotnet build src/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons.csproj -v minimal -p:OutputPath=$PWD/.scratch-build/ -p:AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath=false` (then rm -rf .scratch-build), and separately keep retrying a plain `dotnet build ...` (no OutputPath override) to actually deploy once the lock clears. (2) Every closed chunk of work gets `workflow ticket new --repo GTFO.AbsurdWeapons --type fix|feature|docs --summary \"...\" --status closed` then staged+committed per ticket (split hunks across shared files like GunInjector.cs/Plugin.cs/SeekerGuns.cs when two tickets land in the same file - use `git stash push --keep-index -u`, or revert-to-HEAD-then-reapply-hunks, to isolate). (3) Built a small reusable .NET reflection tool at the session scratchpad ($SCRATCH/reflect, a System.Reflection.Metadata/PortableExecutable console app) to read exact method signatures/field types/enum values straight out of GTFOs BepInEx interop DLLs (BepInEx/interop/Modules-ASM.dll, Wwise-ASM.dll) whenever guessing at an undocumented game API - this is how the Tentacle Cannon zero-damage bug and the Shrink Beam sound event names were found; reuse/rebuild this tool rather than guessing at interop APIs blind. (4) Rocket Launcher`s DamageUtil.DoExplosionDamage player-splash-damage call was removed once on suspicion it caused a screen-blinding black-box bug, then the user explicitly asked for it back since no simpler verified per-player damage API exists (Dam_PlayerDamageBase only exposes complex native-packet Receive*Damage methods) - its restored and the user accepts the residual risk. (5) v1 documentation pass is DONE and committed (G.AWPN-T96): README.md, package/README.md, package/CHANGELOG.md, package/manifest.json, docs/design/weapon-references.md all rewritten against current source. (6) The user runs multiple Claude Code windows at once and sometimes pastes a message meant for a different window into this one (has happened twice, confirmed by the user saying \"wrong window\") - if a message is unrelated to GTFO.AbsurdWeapons weapon work, ask before acting on it instead of guessing. (7) G.AWPN-T89 (find a real rocket-model game asset to replace the hand-built capsule) is open and explicitly deferred - do not work it until the user says when.",
    "state":  "Repo is clean except the uncommitted Shrink Beam loop-sound change described above (Sounds.cs + ShrinkBeam.cs) and untracked .prose/agent-session.json* files (unrelated, leave alone). Most recent commits on main: G.AWPN-T96 (v1 docs pass), G.AWPN-T95 (Rocket Launcher player-damage restored + smoke-\u003edust description fix), G.AWPN-T92 (weapon rework session 4: rocket dust trail, Shadow Dagger end-of-stealth flicker + 0.25s kill bonus, Shrink Beam barrel-tracking + 25%/40%/0.6m thresholds, Warhammer crater debris), G.AWPN-T91 (Tentacle Cannon zero-damage fix - it is the only gun on a ShotgunRanged archetype so weaponRayData.damage silently arrives as 0 for it; now reads GunInjector.TentacleDamage.Value directly, corrected to 25 with a ConfigMigrations entry for the shipped-100 default). Noticed but NOT touched: tickets G.AWPN-T93/T94 (open, from a different window) about splitting Hand Grenade into its own standalone mod repo. Build command for this project: `dotnet build src/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons.csproj -v minimal` (deploys straight into the live BepInEx profile plugins folder); tests: `dotnet test tests/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons.Tests/GTFO.AbsurdWeapons.Tests.csproj -v minimal` (39 tests, all passing).",
    "next":  "1. Wait for the user to confirm the Shrink Beam loop sound is good in-game; once confirmed, file a closed feature ticket and commit Sounds.cs + ShrinkBeam.cs together. 2. Keep responding to live-playtest feedback in the same rapid fix-build-deploy-report loop this whole session has used; batch related small changes into one ticket+commit at natural pauses (e.g. when the user closes the game) rather than one commit per tiny tweak. 3. Leave G.AWPN-T89 (rocket model asset search) untouched until the user explicitly asks for it. 4. If a mid-session message seems unrelated to this GTFO.AbsurdWeapons mod, check whether its meant for a different Claude Code window before acting on it.",
